-- title:
--   Layers of constants: discrete valuation rings, uniformisers, completions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, meaning $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element of $A$, and assume the contracted ring $A\cap k_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ and with algebraically closed residue field, and that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some element of $A\cap k_0$. Assume further $\varpi_t\in k_0\cap A$ satisfies $\varpi_t^{q^2-1}=q\,u$ for a unit $u$ of $A$. Let $(K_l)_{l\in\iota}$ be finite extensions of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, each equipped with a valuation subring $A_l$ whose members are exactly the elements lying in $A$; let $n_0$ be an index with $K_{n_0}\le K_l$ for all $l$; let $\pi_t\in A$ satisfy $\pi_t^{q^2-1}=q$; and assume every $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb Q$ (the image of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition subgroup) whose tame character at $\pi_t$, the residue in $A$ of $\tau(\pi_t)/\pi_t$ when that quotient lies in $A$ and $0$ otherwise, equals $1$, fixes $K_{n_0}$ pointwise. Then for all $E_0\ge 1$ and all $w_0$ such that $\pi_0^{E_0}=\varpi_t^{w_0}v$ for some $v\in k_0$ with $v,v^{-1}\in A$, there are subrings $C'_l\subseteq A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that are domains and discrete valuation rings, elements $\varpi'_l\in C'_l$, rings $W_l$ that are domains, discrete valuation rings and complete for the adic topology of their maximal ideals, elements $\pi_l\in W_l$, natural numbers $e_l$, and ring homomorphisms $j_l\colon C'_l\to W_l$, such that: $C'_l$ consists exactly of the elements of $A$ lying in $K_l$; an element $d$ of $C'_l$ has residue $0$ in the residue field of $A$ iff $d\in\varpi'_lC'_l$; $C'_{n_0}\subseteq C'_l$ for all $l$; $\varpi'_{n_0}\ne 0$; every element of $A$ is algebraic over $C'_{n_0}$; each $\pi_l$ is irreducible and $e_l\ge 1$; every inertia element with tame character $1$ at $\pi_t$ fixes $\varpi'_{n_0}$; there are $w\ge 1$ and a unit $v$ of $A$ with $(\varpi'_{n_0})^{e_{n_0}E_0}=v\,\pi_t^{\,w}$ in $A$; for each $l$ there is $v\in C'_l$ with $v^{-1}\in C'_l$ and $\pi_0=v\,(\varpi'_l)^{e_l}$; $j_l(\varpi'_l)=\pi_l$; $j_l(c)\in(\pi_l^n)$ implies $c\in((\varpi'_l)^n)$ for all $n$; and every element of $W_l$ is congruent to some $j_l(c)$ modulo $\pi_l^n$ for every $n$.
--
--   This is the constants-tower input for the layered presentations of the semistable model at a node: it produces, from a tower of finite layers $K_l$ over a field of admissible small constants $k_0$, the layerwise discrete valuation rings $A\cap K_l$ (by Krull–Akizuki, via [`ValuationSubring.isDiscreteValuationRing_of_algebraMap_mem_of_finite`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.isDiscreteValuationRing_of_algebraMap_mem_of_finite)), their uniformisers and ramification indices over $\pi_0$, and their completions with uniformiser-compatible, dense-to-all-orders embeddings (via [`IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_isAdicComplete_map_maximalIdeal_eq_forall_sub_mem_maximalIdeal`](thm.html#IsDiscreteValuationRing.exists_isAdicComplete_map_maximalIdeal_eq_forall_sub_mem_maximalIdeal)), together with the tame-inertia invariance of the bottom uniformiser and its relation to $\pi_t$. It is used by the three node-core constructions [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.klevel_nodeCore_nodeCharts_hasseGerm_nodeCentre_of_affineChart_poles_hasse_commonChart_nodes_igusaSep) and its variants for $q=3$ and $q=2$.
